tools/wb_serve.cpp EOF (W906-1203REOPEN): boot open failure -> fault + WAR16150 at the first tick; module check kAlarm (after its WAR16154) -> the problems' ring mask; kPass -> recovered; W906_Pci1203ReopenTick in the main loop next to the link watch: when stopped (not SystemStart, no HOME step, no web HOME job, no 1203 axis in a motion state) it does what EtherCAT/Pci1203Reopen.h asks -- kCmdRingReset (the problem rings) or kCmdCardRescan -- with WB_1203_OPEN_WAIT_SEC set to 5 s for that call (Open() otherwise waits up to 90 s on the serve loop), then fAllMotorHome = false, starts the IO thread if the card is open and it is not running, and arms a new module-check generation; 3 failed tries -> WAR16157 (notice). pci1203.card.reopen (the page button) -> 3 more tries, refused while running. Same-line hooks at the boot "card NOT opened" branch, the module check kAlarm / kPass lines, the main loop, and W906_Dispatch1203Ex. D:\HT9045\Error\AlarmCodeList.txt gets WAR16157 (machine data, backed up). Web part in the web commit of the same name.

Simulation only (EastSun): the decision (22) and the command (Pci1203Pure 106) are unit-tested; the host wiring is compiled, not run on the card. Not done: after a ring-1 reset the IO outputs restart at 0 until the engine next writes them; the link watch may still raise WAR16152 if the card stays closed > 10 s. readonly / control gates PASS; code-after-comment scan 0. Debug + release (affected targets). WORKLOG section 2 row 144.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
